Answer 1: The McCabe features, related to control flow and code complexity, include v(g) (cyclomatic complexity), ev(g) (essential complexity), iv(g) (design complexity), and branchCount. These are typically indicative of structural complexity and the likelihood of defects due to increased testing and debugging challenges. For example, higher values of v(g) or branchCount often correlate with higher defect rates. Additionally, design_to_cyclomatic_ratio and essential_to_cyclomatic_ratio highlight structuredness and clarity.

